        905
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "παύσα-σθαι, ‘to stop (oneself), cease’\nTo form the first aorist infinitive middle, add -[α]σθαι to the aorist stem, e.g.\nἐ-παυσá-μην, ‘I stopped (myself)’ > stem: παυσα- > παύσα-σθαι, ‘to stop\n(oneself), cease’",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "box",
      "order": 11,
      "bbox": [
        769,
        82,
        915,
        907
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Forms\n• Observe once again the familiar first aorist stem in -σα- (cf. aorist indicatives\n  131).\n• The first aorist active infinitive ending in -[σ]αι may look odd, but you have\n  already met -αι as an infinitive ending in e.g. εἶν-αι, ‘to be’, ἰέν-αι, ‘to go’,\n  and εἰδέν-αι, ‘to know’.\n• In the middle infinitive, the ending -σθαι is the same as in the present infini-\n  tive (παύ-ε-σθαι).",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": "■",
